-- title:
--   Pl-points reducing into C₂ off C₁ meet the smooth locus
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and let $K\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ be the intermediate field $L$-generated by the image of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81); write $X=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) for the pushout of the two chart morphisms and $\pi=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) $: X\to \operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed proper and flat, with base change to $L$ smooth of relative dimension $1$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$. Let $c_1:C_1\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and $c_2:C_2\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $i_1,i_2$ be closed immersions of $C_1$, $C_2$ into the fibre product $X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}k$ over $\operatorname{Spec}k$ (so $i_m$ followed by the second projection is $c_m$), such that every point of the fibre product lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced, and its underlying set is finite of cardinality $n>0$. Let $U$ be an open subscheme of $X$ smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $A$ and containing every such open. Let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $Pl$, let $\rho:A\to Pl$ be a ring map inducing the structure map $A\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $\pi_k:Pl\to k$ be a surjective ring map with $\pi_k\circ\rho$ the structure map $A\to k$. The conclusion: for every morphism $\xi:\operatorname{Spec}Pl\to X$ with $\xi$ followed by $\pi$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\rho$, and every $k$-point $c:\operatorname{Spec}k\to C_2$ (a section of $c_2$), if the composite of $c$, $i_2$ and the first projection $X_k\to X$ equals $\xi\circ\operatorname{Spec}\pi_k$, and the image of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}k$ under $i_2\circ c$ does not lie in the image of $i_1$, then the set-theoretic image of $\xi$ is contained in $U$.
--
--   This is the step in the analysis of the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$ asserting that a $Pl$-valued point whose reduction is a $k$-point of the component $C_2$ away from its intersection with $C_1$ already factors through the maximal open subscheme that is smooth of relative dimension one over $A$; it is the counterpart, with the roles of $C_1$ and $C_2$ exchanged, of the corresponding statement for $C_1$. It is used in the constructions of sections and in the computations of divisor classes and reductions attached to points of the model.
